WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.840
Virginia's state fossil is a scallop shell.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.220
It is millions of years old.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.620
Yet it looks a lot like a scallop shell on a beach today.

4
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.640
How do scientists know that living things have changed over time, and are related?

5
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:22.433
A fossil is the preserved remains or traces of a living thing from the past.

6
00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:26.133
Shells, bones, teeth and footprints can all be fossils.

7
00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:31.573
Fossils are rare, so the fossil record, all the fossils found so far, has gaps.

8
00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:35.753
Even so, it shows many kinds of life that are not alive now.

9
00:00:36.573 --> 00:00:39.373
A group is extinct when no living members are left.

10
00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.273
Trilobites are extinct.

11
00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.927
Here is one well-known early fossil for each group.

12
00:00:45.787 --> 00:00:47.227
It is not the oldest one found.

13
00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:51.187
Early fish, about 518 million years old.

14
00:00:52.027 --> 00:00:55.147
Four-legged animals, about 365 million.

15
00:00:56.247 --> 00:00:58.647
Mammal relatives, about 205 million.

16
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:02.267
Bird-like dinosaurs, about 150 million.

17
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:08.670
Your arm has one upper arm bone, two lower arm bones, wrist bones and finger bones.

18
00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:13.230
A cat's front leg, a whale's flipper and a bat's wing have the same set.

19
00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.970
The shapes differ, and the jobs differ.

20
00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.410
A common ancestor is an early population.

21
00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.730
Two or more kinds of living things came from it.

22
00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.690
A shared ancestor with these bones explains the match best.

23
00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:29.563
DNA gives a second check.

24
00:01:30.403 --> 00:01:35.523
A DNA sequence is the order of the bases A, T, C and G along a piece of DNA.

25
00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.583
Small changes in DNA happen and get passed on.

26
00:01:40.523 --> 00:01:45.003
Species that split from a common ancestor more recently have had less time to

27
00:01:45.003 --> 00:01:49.643
collect changes. So closer relatives usually have more similar DNA.

28
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:56.197
In science, a theory is a well-tested explanation backed by many lines of evidence.

29
00:01:57.037 --> 00:01:58.037
It is not a guess.

30
00:01:58.797 --> 00:02:03.077
The theory of evolution says living things change over time and share common

31
00:02:03.077 --> 00:02:08.917
ancestors. It predicts that fossils, bones and DNA will tell the same family story.

32
00:02:09.917 --> 00:02:11.657
Each one could have told a different story.

33
00:02:12.557 --> 00:02:13.937
Instead, they largely agree.

34
00:02:14.677 --> 00:02:16.137
That is how scientists know.
